WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.169 --> 00:00:03.370
In this part of level editing,

2
00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:05.769
I want to talk about building the mini-map.

3
00:00:05.769 --> 00:00:07.769
Now, there are a couple of things that we need to do

4
00:00:07.769 --> 00:00:12.769
in order to get our world partition mini-map to work.

5
00:00:12.929 --> 00:00:16.730
And that setup's actually fairly easy.

6
00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:19.789
It just is not well known.

7
00:00:19.789 --> 00:00:21.449
And the one thing that we really need to do

8
00:00:21.449 --> 00:00:22.530
is put in something called

9
00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:24.829
the world partition mini-map volume.

10
00:00:24.829 --> 00:00:26.609
Once you place this into our level,

11
00:00:26.609 --> 00:00:28.690
we should scale it to the size of our landscape.

12
00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:30.969
And this is really gonna help us ensure

13
00:00:30.969 --> 00:00:35.329
that we are only capturing the area that we want.

14
00:00:35.329 --> 00:00:38.850
Inside of our world partition mini-map

15
00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.450
that is placed inside of our level, we can select that

16
00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:44.450
and then we're gonna have a bunch of different options.

17
00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:47.770
Under here, we have things like our world unit per pixel

18
00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:52.859
or which allows us to increase or decrease

19
00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:56.000
the size of the capture and world units

20
00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.060
that we are going to capture.

21
00:00:58.060 --> 00:00:59.740
We then have our builder cell size

22
00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:03.520
which allows us to adjust the size of the individual grids

23
00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:05.280
that are used when we grid this up

24
00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:07.819
and build the sections for it

25
00:01:07.819 --> 00:01:10.500
as this isn't built as one giant texture

26
00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:13.540
but it is built with virtual textures in mind.

27
00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.859
So it is built in quadrants

28
00:01:15.859 --> 00:01:18.620
and then streamed in as one massive texture.

29
00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:21.540
Underneath build cell size, we have capture source

30
00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:23.739
which allows us to do many different things.

31
00:01:23.739 --> 00:01:25.620
You notice that it is a dropdown menu.

32
00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:26.620
And from this menu,

33
00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:29.219
we can select a whole bunch of different options

34
00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:33.099
in terms of how the mini-map texture is actually output.

35
00:01:33.099 --> 00:01:35.579
Last but not least, we have capture warmup frames.

36
00:01:35.579 --> 00:01:38.180
And if you notice, this is actually set to 10

37
00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:40.209
in this example.

38
00:01:40.209 --> 00:01:43.409
This allows things like world partition,

39
00:01:43.409 --> 00:01:47.370
Nanite and other systems time to stream in

40
00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:50.769
and warm up as the capture happens

41
00:01:50.769 --> 00:01:55.090
and eliminates seams that could be shown

42
00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:56.650
inside the ending artwork.

43
00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:58.530
So let's pop over to the editor now

44
00:01:58.609 --> 00:01:59.849
and check out how this works.

45
00:01:59.849 --> 00:02:01.890
So first off, what we're gonna do

46
00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:06.689
is I have a world partition mini-map here.

47
00:02:06.689 --> 00:02:07.769
So this is the mini-map

48
00:02:07.769 --> 00:02:09.969
and this is gonna be added by default.

49
00:02:09.969 --> 00:02:12.030
But what we need to do is come in here

50
00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:16.520
and add a mini world partition mini-map volume.

51
00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:17.900
And for me, what I'm gonna do

52
00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:19.520
is I'm going to zero this out

53
00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:21.719
and then I'm gonna hit F to kind of focus in on this.

54
00:02:21.719 --> 00:02:26.240
And we want this to cover our entire massive landscape.

55
00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:28.280
So we're gonna scale this thing.

56
00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:32.139
Actually, I'm probably gonna do something like this.

57
00:02:35.599 --> 00:02:39.439
And let's do, well, probably need to be like 5,000,

58
00:02:39.439 --> 00:02:43.349
I think.

59
00:02:43.349 --> 00:02:45.050
Well, 5,000 is a little bit too much.

60
00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:47.990
So let's just scale this back in.

61
00:02:47.990 --> 00:02:53.020
We'll say like 2,500

62
00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:54.740
and keep scaling this in just a little bit.

63
00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:56.900
We want it right on the edges there.

64
00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:59.460
Looks about right, so about 2,000

65
00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:02.229
and then we're gonna do the same thing over here.

66
00:03:02.229 --> 00:03:06.300
So probably just scale this out to 2,000.

67
00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:09.539
And then here, we're gonna do like 500

68
00:03:09.539 --> 00:03:12.240
and we wanna make sure that,

69
00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:14.590
yeah, that looks about good.

70
00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:16.330
We wanna make sure that this is not,

71
00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:18.250
there's nothing like sticking out

72
00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:21.719
or sticking not covered by the volume

73
00:03:21.719 --> 00:03:22.759
of bottom of the volume,

74
00:03:22.759 --> 00:03:24.520
but also nothing not covered by the top.

75
00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:27.659
We don't want like this part of the landscape

76
00:03:27.659 --> 00:03:29.219
sticking out of the top or it'll get cut off.

77
00:03:29.219 --> 00:03:31.360
We wanna make sure everything is inside of there.

78
00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:32.240
So there we go.

79
00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:33.639
We have that all set up.

80
00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:35.199
This is great.

81
00:03:35.199 --> 00:03:36.039
So the next thing that we're gonna do

82
00:03:36.039 --> 00:03:38.560
is we're gonna come down to our,

83
00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:39.639
or I shouldn't say come down,

84
00:03:39.639 --> 00:03:42.520
but we're gonna locate our World Partition Minimap.

85
00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:43.439
There we go.

86
00:03:43.439 --> 00:03:45.759
And then what I'm gonna do is say my warmup features,

